# The glTF conformance corpus: what Blix's reader is checked against, and where each file comes from.
#
# ── Why a manifest and not the bytes ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventions §7 says the SPECIFICATION is the requirement and owning an asset that
# exercises it is a download, not a precondition. So what is banked here is the
# KNOWLEDGE — which asset, from which commit, and what it proves — and the bytes stay
# a fetch. That also keeps three upstream licences (per-model CC0/CC-BY for the Khronos
# samples, Apache-2.0 for the generator and Cesium) out of this repo's history: the
# fetcher pulls each Sample-Assets model's own LICENSE.md down beside it.
#
# Commits are PINNED. An unpinned corpus is not a control — upstream can change an
# asset under you and the diff shows up as a Blix regression.
#
#   tools/fetch-gltf-corpus.sh                 # everything
#   tools/fetch-gltf-corpus.sh vertexcolor     # only lines matching a substring
#
# Fetched into third_party/gltf-corpus/, which is gitignored.
#
# ── Format ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   source   <key> <pinned base url>
#   sample   <Name> [variant] [files...]        variant defaults to glTF-Binary/<Name>.glb
#   generator <Group> <lo>-<hi> [extra files...]
#   negative <Group> <lo>-<hi>
#   cesium   <Name> <variant> <files...>
# Everything after a trailing '#' is what the asset is FOR. Keep it — an asset whose
# purpose nobody recorded gets deleted by the next person who tidies up.

source SA https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Sample-Assets/90d7ede14c7e280af263824604b427a1ca02cb66
source AG https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Asset-Generator/3d99767e9a67fbfe109f0d298c1e8d909bcac9db
source CS https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CesiumGS/cesium/08a0d8db4bb800664e447002e7af7d85bade3c29

# ── Khronos glTF-Sample-Assets — realistic models. "Does this asset look right." ──

sample BoxVertexColors          # COLOR_0 is a BASE-COLOUR MULTIPLIER. Rendered white until I-A; the asset that settled it against 33 nature-kit primitives that all use COLOR_0 as baked AO.
sample AlphaBlendModeTest       # The MASK/BLEND/OPAQUE matrix with real alpha. The nature kit could not show this: all 26 of its MASK materials have baseAlpha 1.0, so a faithful cutout discards nothing.
sample MultiUVTest glTF MultiUVTest.gltf MultiUVTest.bin uv0.png uv1.png   # TEXCOORD_1. The fetcher derives MultiUVTest_uv1.gltf from this — see below.
sample MorphPrimitivesTest      # Morph targets, which Blix does NOT read. Kept as the standing negative: GltfIgnored must keep reporting them.
sample NormalTangentTest        # TANGENT alongside a normal map.
sample SimpleSparseAccessor glTF SimpleSparseAccessor.gltf SimpleSparseAccessor.bin   # Sparse accessors. Correct since before the inlet arc; kept so it stays that way.
sample RiggedSimple             # The smallest real skin — 2 joints, 1 mesh.
sample RiggedFigure             # A skin with a hierarchy under it.
sample AnimatedMorphCube        # Animation channels targeting morph weights: channels Blix must ignore without mis-reading the rest of the animation.
sample TextureCoordinateTest    # Which texCoord set each texture names, drawn so a wrong set is visible rather than subtle.
sample BoxInterleaved           # Interleaved POSITION/NORMAL in one buffer view.
sample OrientationTest          # Node transform composition. A sign error here reads as "the model is fine, the scene is wrong".

# ── Animation and skins. Added for the node-animation arc: glTF animates NODES — joints, and any ──
# other node — and until it, Blix read clips only on skin 0's joints and could not animate a
# rigid part at all. Each line says which reading it separates.
sample AnimatedTriangle glTF-Embedded AnimatedTriangle.gltf   # Rotation on a plain mesh node, no skin: node animation in its smallest form.
sample BoxAnimated              # Translation and rotation on a node hierarchy of rigid meshes. A reader that animates only joints draws it frozen.
sample InterpolationTest        # STEP, LINEAR and CUBICSPLINE on T, R and S, side by side: the sampler, read or not.
sample CesiumMilkTruck          # Rigid wheels spun by node animation under a moving parent.
sample SimpleSkin glTF-Embedded SimpleSkin.gltf   # The tutorial skin: two joints, one clip, every value readable by hand.
sample CesiumMan                # The classic walking skin; joints under a transformed parent.
sample Fox                      # A skin with three clips, and a mesh node that is not where the skeleton hangs.
sample BrainStem                # Many meshes on many skins over one skeleton: the multi-skin case that poses every skin from one clip.
sample RecursiveSkeletons       # Skins that reuse joints of other skins, and joints that are also skinned meshes' parents — the case the tags call issues.
sample SimpleMorph glTF-Embedded SimpleMorph.gltf   # Morph targets with animated weights. Blix does NOT read morphs; kept so the refusal to mis-read stays checked.
sample MorphStressTest          # Many morph targets and a weights clip beside ordinary content.
sample AnimatedColorsCube       # KHR_animation_pointer on a material colour: a channel whose target is not a node.
# ── Spec breadth. Added for the spec-support audit: one asset per corner a reader can get ──
# wrong silently. Each is judged against its own README's expected picture.
sample MetalRoughSpheres        # The metallic x roughness matrix, textured.
sample MetalRoughSpheresNoTextures # The same matrix from factors alone.
sample NormalTangentMirrorTest  # Authored tangents with mirrored UVs: the frame's handedness, per seam.
sample TextureSettingsTest      # Sampler wrap and filter modes, each labelled.
sample TextureTransformMultiTest # KHR_texture_transform on several channels at once.
sample TextureEncodingTest      # PNG/JPEG, 8/16-bit, sRGB/linear decode paths.
sample TextureLinearInterpolationTest # Filtering in linear, not sRGB, space.
sample VertexColorTest          # COLOR_0 in its encodings next to a textured control.
sample NegativeScaleTest        # Mirrored nodes: winding and normals under a negative determinant.
sample MeshPrimitiveModes glTF-Embedded MeshPrimitiveModes.gltf   # POINTS, LINES, LINE_LOOP, LINE_STRIP, TRIANGLE_STRIP, TRIANGLE_FAN.
sample TriangleWithoutIndices glTF-Embedded TriangleWithoutIndices.gltf   # A primitive with no index accessor.
sample MultipleScenes glTF-Embedded MultipleScenes.gltf   # Two scenes; which one a reader shows is the default scene's to say.
sample Cameras glTF-Embedded Cameras.gltf   # Perspective and orthographic cameras, which a viewer may use or ignore but must not mis-read.
sample SimpleInstancing         # EXT_mesh_gpu_instancing: one mesh drawn many times by one node.
sample NodeVisibilityTest       # KHR_node_visibility.
sample EmissiveStrengthTest     # KHR_materials_emissive_strength: emission past 1.0 — the glowing-bulb case.
sample DamagedHelmet            # Every core PBR channel on one real asset.
sample BoomBox                  # Occlusion, roughness and metalness packed in one image, beside emission.
sample Unicode❤♻Test            # A path and names outside ASCII.
sample CompareBaseColor         # The Compare* PBR tests: one parameter varied per row, each against its README.
sample CompareMetallic
sample CompareRoughness
sample CompareNormal
sample CompareAmbientOcclusion
sample CompareAlphaCoverage
sample CompareEmissiveStrength
sample CompareSheen
sample CompareClearcoat
sample CompareTransmission
sample CompareVolume
sample CompareIor
sample CompareSpecular
sample CompareIridescence
sample CompareAnisotropy
sample CompareDispersion
# ── Material extensions. Added when the importer went from reading 2 of the 13 that ──
# SharpGLTF surfaces to reading all of them. Before this the corpus declared NOTHING that
# exercised a KHR_materials_* extension, which is the §7 failure in its purest form: the
# engine's capability was being set by an accident of what had been downloaded, and the
# sentence "no asset needs it" would have been true and meaningless.
sample SheenChair               # KHR_materials_sheen with both channels textured. The fabric lobe metallic-roughness cannot express, and the reason a curtain reads as cloth.
sample DiffuseTransmissionTeacup # KHR_materials_diffuse_transmission: light SCATTERED through a thin surface. The extension a leaf and a curtain actually want, as opposed to clear-pane transmission.
sample TransmissionTest         # KHR_materials_transmission across a factor sweep, which is the one extension the importer already read — kept so it stays read.
sample DragonAttenuation        # KHR_materials_volume: thickness and attenuation, which the spec says are meaningless without transmission. The pair, so the dependency is exercised rather than assumed.
sample ClearCoatTest            # KHR_materials_clearcoat, including the clearcoat NORMAL channel — a second normal map on one material, which is where a reader that assumes one goes wrong.
sample IridescenceLamp          # KHR_materials_iridescence: factor, IOR, and a thickness RANGE rather than a scalar.
sample AnisotropyBarnLamp       # KHR_materials_anisotropy: strength and rotation.
sample SpecularTest             # KHR_materials_specular: dielectric F0 strength and tint without lying about metalness.
sample UnlitTest                # KHR_materials_unlit, which is a whole shading model rather than a parameter — the standing check that a flag is not read as a factor.

# ── Khronos glTF-Asset-Generator — permutation matrices. Each group DECLARES its ──
# expected result, so "all N render the same" is a real assertion rather than a hope.
# Pair every such claim with a control that the renders are not uniformly blank:
# six identical WHITE images also agree with each other.

generator Mesh_PrimitiveVertexColor 0-5                                   # All six COLOR_0 spellings (float/ushort/ubyte x VEC3/VEC4). Verified byte-identical against a control of 415,625 strongly coloured pixels.
generator Material_AlphaMask 0-5 Textures/BaseColor_Plane.png             # The cutoff matrix. _05 dims baseColorFactor.a to 0.7, making its EFFECTIVE cutoff 0.571 — which is why ordering these by nominal cutoff is wrong.
generator Material_AlphaBlend 0-6 Textures/BaseColor_Plane.png            # BLEND. The conformance half; ordering within the blended group is still open.
generator Material_DoubleSided 0-4 Textures/BaseColor_Plane.png Textures/Normal_Plane.png   # doubleSided, which is pipeline state in Vulkan and so cannot be a push constant.
generator Mesh_PrimitivesUV 0-8 Textures/BaseColor_Plane.png Textures/Normal_Plane.png   # Multiple primitives with differing UV sets, the case a single "does it have UV1" flag gets wrong.
generator Buffer_Interleaved 0-4 Textures/BaseColor_Grey.png              # Stride. A vertex buffer is walked at the PIPELINE's declared stride, so a mismatch here reads as garbage geometry, not as a missing attribute.
generator Accessor_Sparse 0-3 Textures/BaseColor_A.png Textures/BaseColor_B.png   # Sparse, in every place the spec allows it.
generator Node_NegativeScale 0-12 Textures/BaseColor_Nodes.png Textures/MetallicRoughness_Nodes.png Textures/Normal_Nodes.png   # Negative scale flips winding. Culling is pipeline state, so a determinant sign has to reach the pipeline choice.
generator Animation_Skin 0-11                                             # Skins under animation. Animation channels target NODES, not skins — the thing the importer's clip-ordering guard currently refuses rather than solves.

negative Mesh_NoPosition 0-0        # Must be REFUSED. A reader that invents positions passes every positive test.
negative Mesh_PrimitiveRestart 0-0  # Must be REFUSED. Primitive restart is not in glTF.

# ── Cesium — engine-hardening oddities nothing else carries ─────────────────────

cesium BoxInterleaved glTF BoxInterleaved.gltf BoxInterleaved.bin   # A second interleaving, authored by a different tool than the Khronos one.
cesium BoxInterleavedTranslucent glTF BoxInterleavedTranslucent.gltf BoxInterleavedTranslucent.bin   # Interleaved AND blended, which is the combination that finds a stride bug in the blend pipeline specifically.
cesium BoxNoNormals glTF BoxNoNormals.gltf                          # NO NORMAL attribute. The spec says generate flat normals; Blix's behaviour here is unasserted.
cesium BoxInverted glTF BoxInverted.gltf                            # Inverted winding.
cesium BoxBackFaceCulling glTF BoxBackFaceCulling.gltf              # Culling as authored.
cesium BoxCutout glTF BoxCutout.gltf                                # A cutout from outside the Khronos matrices.
cesium BoxVertexColorsDracoRGB glTF-Draco BoxVertexColorsDracoRGB.gltf   # Draco. Blix does NOT decode it; this asset exists so the refusal is CHECKED rather than assumed.
cesium BoxWeb3dQuantizedAttributes glTF BoxWeb3dQuantizedAttributes.gltf # Quantized attributes via an extension Blix does not implement.
cesium BoxTexturedKtx2Basis glTF-Binary BoxTexturedKtx2Basis.glb    # KTX2/Basis textures, likewise unimplemented and likewise worth failing predictably.
cesium CesiumMan glTF-Draco CesiumMan.gltf 0.bin CesiumMan.jpg      # A Draco-compressed SKIN.

# ── Locally derived ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Assets that do not exist upstream, expressed as the EDIT rather than as bytes.
#
#   MultiUVTest_uv1.gltf — MultiUVTest with baseColorTexture.texCoord set to 1.
#     Upstream ships the second UV set but no material that NAMES it, so the stock
#     asset cannot tell a reader that honours texCoord from one that always samples
#     set 0. One key of difference; see tools/fetch-gltf-corpus.sh.
#
# ── The gap this corpus still does NOT cover ───────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here exercises JOINTS_1 / more than four influences per vertex. That is the
# one glTF gap whose failure is a WRONG RESULT (a silently truncated skin) rather than
# a missing feature, and it is covered only by a SharpGLTF fixture in Test.Graphics
# section BC. If an upstream asset for it ever appears, it belongs here.
